  "description": "Our system is built on a core schema identified by the base URI **http://example.org/schema**, with a base type of **Entity**. It defines three main types\u2014**Person**, **Place**, and **Organization**\u2014and connects them through the relations **locatedIn**, **memberOf** and **hasPart**; equivalence between entities is expressed with **owl:sameAs**. The API service listens on **0.0.0.0** at port **8080**, exposing its base URL **http://localhost:8080/api** and storing persistent files under **/var/app/data**. Administrative access is secured with the username **admin** and password **s3cr3t**. By default, path traversal follows the **hasPart** relation, while auxiliary \u201chair\u201d relations include **hasHair** and **hasColor**. Sample endpoints you can try are **http://localhost:8080/api/example1** and **http://localhost:8080/api/example2**.\n\nOperational components are fully enabled: statistical collection runs daily according to the cron expression **0 0 * * ***. We use a Redis broker at **redis.local:6379** with a task queue named **taskQueue** that can hold up to **10000** items, an Elasticsearch cluster at **es.local:9200**, and a Neo4j graph database at **neo4j.local:7687** accessed with user **neo4j** and password **password123**. The viewer interface is set to English (**en**) in **advanced** mode, uses the colour **#336699**, and accepts image files ending in **jpg**, **png**, or **gif**; no custom logo is configured. Geographic data comes from Geonames for the countries **US**, **CA**, **GB**, with extra URIs at **http://example.org/geonames/extra**, while the TGN hierarchy references parents **http://example.org/tgn/parent1** and **http://example.org/tgn/parent2**. BAG storage connects to a PostgreSQL instance on **bagdb.local:5432**, using the credentials **baguser** / **bagpass** and the database named **bagdb**. Import processes watch the local directories **/data/import1** and **/data/import2**, and also pull from S3 (region **us\u2011east\u20111**, access key **AKIAEXAMPLE**, secret **abcd1234example**) in the buckets **my-bucket1** and **my-bucket2**; differences are visualised with **meld**. Finally, the project\u2019s branding images are available at **http://example.org/logo1.png** and **http://example.org/logo2.png**."
